---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Where does my code go? EpicScan data handling"
  description="Hosted EpicScan scans run on our own Mac Studio machines in the Czech Republic. Or run the open-source scanner on your own infrastructure."
  path="/privacy-and-data"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container hero-inner" style="gap: 20px;">
      <h1 class="h1">Where does my code go?</h1>
      <p class="lead">Only where you choose. Hosted scans run on hardware we own and operate in the Czech Republic. Self-hosted scans never leave your network.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding: 24px 0 72px;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid" style="--min: 250px;">
        <article class="card">
          <span class="icon-tile" style="background: rgba(129,140,248,0.12); color: var(--indigo-soft);" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="2" y="2" width="20" height="8" rx="2"></rect><rect x="2" y="14" width="20" height="8" rx="2"></rect><line x1="6" y1="6" x2="6.01" y2="6"></line><line x1="6" y1="18" x2="6.01" y2="18"></line></svg></span>
          <h2 style="font-size: 18px;">Our own hardware</h2>
          <p>Hosted scans run on Mac Studio machines owned and operated by Epicworks s.r.o. in the Czech Republic. No third-party AI service sees your code.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="icon-tile" style="background: rgba(52,211,153,0.12); color: var(--green);" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"></path></svg></span>
          <h2 style="font-size: 18px;">Not kept after the scan</h2>
          <p>Your code is used only for the scan you asked for. It is deleted when the scan ends and never used to train models. We keep operational metadata, such as request logs, for up to 30 days.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="icon-tile" style="background: rgba(125,211,252,0.12); color: #7dd3fc;" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><line x1="2" y1="12" x2="22" y2="12"></line><path d="M12 2a15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4 10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1-4-10 15.3 15.3 0 0 1 4-10z"></path></svg></span>
          <h2 style="font-size: 18px;">Under EU law</h2>
          <p>Epicworks s.r.o. is a Czech company and processes data under the GDPR.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="icon-tile" style="background: rgba(251,191,36,0.12); color: #fbbf24;" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M3 9l9-7 9 7v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"></path><polyline points="9 22 9 12 15 12 15 22"></polyline></svg></span>
          <h2 style="font-size: 18px;">Or keep it on-prem</h2>
          <p>The scanner is open source (Apache-2.0). Run it on your own machines against your own model endpoint (in testing), and your code never leaves your network.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="prose container">
      <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">What we receive in a hosted scan</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The changed files and the minimum surrounding code needed for context.</li>
        <li>The pull or merge request number and repository name, to post the report.</li>
        <li>Never your secrets or CI variables.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Open source and attribution</h2>
      <p>EpicScan is built on <a href="https://github.com/Huge/nano-analyzer" rel="noopener">nano-analyzer</a>, the open-source scanner created by AISLE and released under Apache-2.0, extended by us. EpicScan is inspired by, but not connected in any business way with, AISLE.</p>
      <p><a href="/legal/privacy">Read the privacy policy</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
